Icons of JetBrains (IntelliJ Platform)

The SVG files in this folder are taken, unchanged, from the repository
https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community
at the commit 5540e0d7a9d8c9210c747369ab2e5000434c420d (2026-11-18).

Copyright 2000-2026 JetBrains s.r.o. and contributors.
The files are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the file LICENSE in this folder).
Most of them say so in a comment at their top: "Use of this source code is governed by the Apache 2.0 license."
The repository's own NOTICE.txt says:

  This software includes code from IntelliJ IDEA
  Copyright (C) JetBrains s.r.o.
  https://www.jetbrains.com/idea/

Where each file is from (the name of a file here is the name it has there, without the folder):

- go.svg, kotlin.svg, php.svg, python.svg, ruby.svg, rust.svg and scala.svg: platform/icons/src/language/
- every other .svg: platform/icons/src/expui/fileTypes/ (the icons of the New UI, the light ones)

The files were not changed. The files that the app does not use are not taken.
The app draws them in the file pane of the Orca screen (A-18, src-tauri/src/orca_icon.rs).

About LICENSE. It is the text of the Apache License 2.0 as it is in LICENSE.txt of the tag idea/2026.1.1 of that repository.
The LICENSE.txt at the commit above holds the JetBrains Open-Source Build Terms instead, which refer to the Apache License 2.0 for the open source software of the build.
Why this commit and not a tag: the tags of the releases (idea/2025.2.4 to idea/2026.1.1) hold only 52 of the icons of expui/fileTypes, and the icons of TypeScript, Docker, SQL and the others are there only on the master branch.
